<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-6291] JDBC thin protocol compatibility is broken</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6291</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;After merge &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6118&quot; title=&quot;JDBC Thin: Propagate &amp;quot;lazy&amp;quot; flag&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-6118&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-6118&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5233&quot; title=&quot;JDBC thin Driver: implement metadata support &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-5233&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-5233&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. The JDBC thin protocol compatibility is broken.&lt;br/&gt;
The new client&apos;s handshake cannot be parsed by old servers because the server fails handshake by protocol&apos;s version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, we have to implement compatibility handshake to support this case.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
